      "item": "thm-complex-spin-modules-and-compact-reducibility",
      "finding": "In thm-complex-spin-modules-and-compact-reducibility, step 1.1 chooses a “pairwise orthogonal anisotropic real basis e_1,...,e_n” and separately defines normalized vectors u_i=e_i/√|Q(e_i)|. Step 2.1 nevertheless says “Set ω=i^m e_1⋯e_(2m); the Clifford relations show ω²=1”. For the chosen, potentially unnormalized e_i, the square is ∏Q(e_i), not necessarily 1. In positive dimension two, e_1=2f_1 and e_2=f_2 for an orthonormal basis gives ω²=4, so the asserted p_±=(1±ω)/2 are not idempotents. The proof needs an explicit normalization at this use.",
